WEBVTT

00:01.930 --> 00:04.390
<i>Shizuoka Prefecture semi-finals.</i>

00:04.390 --> 00:08.510
<i>Nankatsu FC faced Shimada FC, who were notable for their strong defense.</i>

00:08.510 --> 00:13.030
<i>They did so without Wakabayashi, who couldn't play because of his injury.</i>

00:13.030 --> 00:15.900
<i>Even though Tsubasa and his friends dominated the game,</i>

00:15.900 --> 00:19.950
<i>Shimada scored after they were able to create a brief opening.</i>

00:23.500 --> 00:28.630
<i>After conceding a second goal later on, Nankatsu found themselves driven into a corner.</i>

00:29.670 --> 00:32.760
<i>However, Tsubasa didn't give up.</i>

00:32.760 --> 00:36.000
<i>With his marvelous passes, he was able to overcome his adversaries,</i>

00:36.000 --> 00:38.680
<i>allowing them to finally score the goal that changed the flow of the game.</i>

00:40.810 --> 00:42.880
<i>Also, thanks to goalkeeper Morisaki's efforts,</i>

00:42.880 --> 00:46.880
<i>Nankatsu FC managed to advance to the finals.</i>

00:48.690 --> 00:56.440
<i>Meanwhile, Meiwa FC also advanced to the finals, thanks to Kojiro Hyuga's return.</i>

01:12.080 --> 01:17.710
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:12.080 --> 01:17.710
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:17.710 --> 01:22.710
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:17.710 --> 01:22.710
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:23.380 --> 01:28.550
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:23.380 --> 01:28.550
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:29.260 --> 01:36.890
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:29.260 --> 01:36.890
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:36.890 --> 01:42.650
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:36.890 --> 01:42.650
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:42.650 --> 01:51.160
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:42.650 --> 01:51.160
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:51.160 --> 01:56.960
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:51.160 --> 01:56.960
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:56.960 --> 02:02.880
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:56.960 --> 02:02.880
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

02:02.880 --> 02:04.380
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:04.380 --> 02:11.680
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:04.380 --> 02:11.680
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:11.680 --> 02:14.600
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

02:11.680 --> 02:14.600
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

02:14.600 --> 02:19.520
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

02:14.600 --> 02:19.520
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:30.420 --> 02:34.420
<b><b>EPISODE 12:
CRUSHING WAKABAYASHI</b></b>

02:33.040 --> 02:36.050
Fight! Fight! Shimizu!

02:36.050 --> 02:39.550
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

02:40.170 --> 02:42.720
<i>Listen to all that cheering!</i>

02:42.720 --> 02:44.450
<i>The day has finally come.</i>

02:44.450 --> 02:46.430
<i>The final match that will decide the Shizuoka Prefecture</i>

02:46.430 --> 02:49.060
<i>representatives for the National Youth Football Tournament begins now!</i>

02:49.060 --> 02:53.000
<i>After this, who will be the team that heads to the National tournament?</i>

02:53.000 --> 02:56.790
<i>Will it be Nankatsu FC, with last year's representative Shutetsu's members at its core,</i>

02:56.790 --> 03:02.570
<i>or the famous Shimizu FC, who have easily defeated their opponents up until now?</i>

03:02.570 --> 03:04.820
All right, I'm ready!

03:05.290 --> 03:07.080
Is your leg really okay?

03:07.080 --> 03:08.500
Of course.

03:08.500 --> 03:11.410
How long did you expect me to sit on the bench, anyway?

03:11.410 --> 03:16.340
Morisaki, you defended our goal well yesterday. Thank you so much.

03:16.340 --> 03:20.840
Leave Nankatsu's goal to me today!

03:22.110 --> 03:26.600
Everyone got that? Our strategy is to thoroughly mark Tsubasa Ozora.

03:26.600 --> 03:29.940
Don't just mark him when he approaches the goal; cover him at every moment,

03:29.940 --> 03:32.880
and prevent him from shooting, passing or dribbling!

03:32.880 --> 03:33.940
Yes!

03:33.940 --> 03:36.040
I'm counting on you, Nakao, Takada.

03:36.040 --> 03:37.860
Right! Leave him to us!

03:43.120 --> 03:47.530
<i>Under the bright summer sun, both teams have lined up on the field.</i>

03:47.530 --> 03:50.450
<i>This final match, the one that will decide the team that will represent the Shizuoka Prefecture...</i>

03:50.450 --> 03:54.250
<i>Nankatsu FC vs. Shimizu FC is about to begin!</i>

03:54.250 --> 03:56.630
So I'm a substitute again?

03:56.630 --> 04:00.140
Hey, Tsubasa! Do your best!

04:00.140 --> 04:04.560
Boss, the game hasn't started yet, so calm down a little.

04:04.560 --> 04:06.040
Shut up!

04:06.040 --> 04:08.460
Today, it's really serious! It's the finals!

04:08.460 --> 04:09.840
When else would I be cheering if—

04:09.840 --> 04:11.420
Tsubasa!

04:12.290 --> 04:16.680
What? Did someone else just cheer Tsubasa...?!

04:16.680 --> 04:18.150
Of course there'll be others...

04:18.150 --> 04:19.980
There are many people here, as you can see.

04:19.980 --> 04:23.990
It's okay if I'm the only one cheering Tsubasa on!

04:24.410 --> 04:27.700
<i>Both teams get into position.</i>

04:27.700 --> 04:30.740
<i>Nankatsu FC will be playing 4-3-3 as always.</i>

04:30.740 --> 04:32.600
<i>The keystones of their offense and defense are</i>

04:32.600 --> 04:35.960
<i>Tsubasa, who has scored a hat-trick in all matches so far,</i>

04:35.960 --> 04:38.310
<i>and their goalkeeper, Wakabayashi.</i>

04:38.310 --> 04:41.080
<i>Wakabayashi didn't participate in the semi-finals,</i>

04:41.080 --> 04:43.210
<i>waiting for this opportunity to participate.</i>

04:43.210 --> 04:47.470
<i>The opponent's team, Shimizu, also rally their defense around their goalkeeper,</i>

04:47.470 --> 04:49.670
<i>Kawakami, to form a solid defense,</i>

04:49.670 --> 04:51.900
<i>and play in a 4-4-2 formation.</i>

04:51.900 --> 04:54.130
<i>Their members are comparable to those of Nankatsu.</i>

04:54.130 --> 04:56.520
<i>They've won their way up to the finals so far.</i>

04:56.520 --> 05:00.720
<i>Both of these teams' average scores per game in each match of the prefectural preliminaries is nearly equal.</i>

05:00.720 --> 05:02.310
<i>Their strength seems to be on the same level, too.</i>

05:02.310 --> 05:05.900
<i>It's safe to say that it's impossible to predict the outcome of this match.</i>

05:06.370 --> 05:09.070
If we win today, we'll be going to the Nationals.

05:09.070 --> 05:11.240
Let's go, Tsubasa.

05:11.240 --> 05:13.040
Yeah!

05:14.510 --> 05:17.710
<i>The match begins with Nankatsu FC's kick-off.</i>

05:18.270 --> 05:20.460
<i>Misaki takes the ball and dashes forward!</i>

05:21.290 --> 05:22.460
Like I'd let you!

05:22.460 --> 05:23.710
Taki!

05:23.710 --> 05:27.380
<i>Misaki lures his opponents and connects a skillful pass.</i>

05:27.380 --> 05:28.220
Tsubasa!

05:28.220 --> 05:31.060
<i>Will Nankatsu be able to get the ball to Tsubasa?</i>

05:32.500 --> 05:36.020
<i>Shimizu is marking Tsubasa with two players!</i>

05:37.270 --> 05:38.520
Watch out, Taki!

05:38.520 --> 05:39.690
I'll be taking that!

05:39.690 --> 05:40.640
Oh no!

05:40.640 --> 05:42.230
<i>Shimizu FC steals the ball!</i>

05:42.230 --> 05:43.610
Run for it, Kanda!

05:43.610 --> 05:46.190
<i>Shimizu is on the fast break with a counter-attack! </i>

05:46.480 --> 05:47.910
Hey, over here!

05:47.910 --> 05:49.780
<i>Kanda rushes into open space!</i>

05:49.780 --> 05:50.950
Fall back!

05:51.470 --> 05:52.320
Kanda!

05:52.320 --> 05:54.160
<i>A long lateral pass! </i>

05:56.540 --> 05:58.160
I won't let you!

05:58.790 --> 06:00.960
<i>Kanda evades it.</i>

06:00.960 --> 06:02.480
<i>As expected of the prestigious Shimizu!</i>

06:02.480 --> 06:04.080
<i>Each player is skilled at their position!</i>

06:04.080 --> 06:06.720
<i>Will Kanda try to get past Takasugi?</i>

06:06.720 --> 06:07.510
You bastard...

06:07.510 --> 06:11.300
<i>Oh, Obayashi and Murakami rush out in front of the goal!</i>

06:11.300 --> 06:12.320
Mark them!

06:12.320 --> 06:12.890
I won't let them!

06:14.390 --> 06:16.890
<i>Kanda passes the ball to Obayashi.</i>

06:18.590 --> 06:19.690
Eat this!

06:19.690 --> 06:21.770
<i>The first shot on goal is from Shimizu...!</i>

06:22.790 --> 06:23.770
Wakabayashi!

06:25.770 --> 06:27.740
<i>Wakabayashi quickly leaps towards the ball!</i>

06:28.660 --> 06:30.860
<i>A perfect save!</i>

06:31.720 --> 06:33.120
Nice catch!

06:34.950 --> 06:37.870
Looks like my leg's in great shape. Tsubasa!

06:38.250 --> 06:40.120
<i>He sends the ball far away.</i>

06:40.120 --> 06:43.040
<i>It's a long pass to Nankatsu's ace striker, Tsubasa.</i>

06:43.760 --> 06:46.130
<i>However, two players are obstinately marking him.</i>

06:47.120 --> 06:48.670
<i>The three of them jump at the same time.</i>

06:48.670 --> 06:54.300
<i>Nankatsu's #10, Tsubasa Ozora, jumps the highest and wins the ball! As to be expected! </i>

06:56.040 --> 06:58.640
<i>Misaki returns the ball with a quick one-touch pass!</i>

06:58.640 --> 07:00.660
<i>Tsubasa takes the ball and dribbles forward!</i>

07:02.810 --> 07:04.770
Go for it, Tsubasa!

07:06.140 --> 07:06.900
Go!

07:06.900 --> 07:10.440
<i>Tsubasa takes a long shot despite the marking!</i>

07:12.320 --> 07:14.780
<i>It smashes against the crossbar! </i>

07:14.780 --> 07:16.240
That was close...

07:16.240 --> 07:17.780
This guy is...

07:17.780 --> 07:18.790
Awesome...

07:22.570 --> 07:23.670
Two won't be enough for him.

07:23.670 --> 07:25.580
Mark him with three players.

07:25.580 --> 07:28.810
Why is there even a crossbar there...?

07:28.810 --> 07:30.300
Tsubasa!

07:30.300 --> 07:33.630
What's wrong? You should have scored that!

07:33.630 --> 07:35.790
Who is that girl?

07:35.790 --> 07:38.890
Boss! Please wait!

07:38.890 --> 07:43.980
Tsubasa! Did you forget me? It's me, Yayoi!

07:44.340 --> 07:46.560
I'm here to cheer you on!

07:46.560 --> 07:47.270
Oh!

07:50.080 --> 07:52.360
Hey, look at me!

07:52.930 --> 07:55.610
What is your relationship with Tsubasa?

07:56.490 --> 07:58.120
What about you?

07:58.120 --> 08:03.610
I'm the leader of the Nankatsu Cheer... No, wait—I'm the commander of Tsubasa's Cheer Squad!

08:03.610 --> 08:07.520
Is that so? I was with Tsubasa in his previous school.

08:07.520 --> 08:09.920
My name is Yayoi Aoba. It's nice to meet you!

08:09.920 --> 08:13.070
I'm a member of the cheering squad. Nice to—ouch!

08:13.070 --> 08:14.930
Stay out of this!

08:15.710 --> 08:18.680
Tsubasa's play is so fine, every time I see him...

08:18.680 --> 08:20.370
He's so lively.

08:23.550 --> 08:28.470
He always used to chase after the ball alone at school.

08:28.470 --> 08:32.280
He kept kicking his football to and from school every day.

08:32.680 --> 08:36.280
But Tsubasa is at his best when he's on the field.

08:37.230 --> 08:41.790
Everyone treated Tsubasa as a weirdo who did nothing but play football.

08:41.790 --> 08:44.040
<i>Seriously, is that kid stupid? </i>

08:44.040 --> 08:49.240
I admired Tsubasa's staunch devotion to football.

08:49.240 --> 08:51.500
<i>Yayoi, we're going ahead! </i>

08:53.600 --> 09:00.010
Yet, before I was able to tell him about my feelings, Tsubasa suddenly transferred.

09:01.070 --> 09:02.530
Hey, shouldn't you be cheering?

09:02.530 --> 09:04.700
Tsubasa got the ball!

09:04.700 --> 09:05.350
Eh?

09:06.320 --> 09:08.350
<i>The pass reaches Tsubasa!</i>

09:10.570 --> 09:13.280
<i>This time around, there are three players marking him.</i>

09:13.280 --> 09:14.530
<i>Three?!</i>

09:15.520 --> 09:17.030
<i>Mark him with three players?</i>

09:17.480 --> 09:18.470
<i>Just as I've said.</i>

09:18.470 --> 09:22.540
<i>But if we do that, the rest of our defense will get weaker...</i>

09:22.540 --> 09:23.950
<i>It'll be alright.</i>

09:23.950 --> 09:29.750
<i>I don't care if the other shoot; I can stop those, even if there are holes in our defense.</i>

09:29.750 --> 09:33.140
<i>Nankatsu really only has him as a finisher.</i>

09:33.140 --> 09:38.680
<i>In other words, if we hold Tsubasa down, there's no way we'll lose!</i>

09:39.630 --> 09:43.260
<i>Being marked by three players must be a first for Tsubasa too.</i>

09:43.260 --> 09:45.850
<i>And with those three being from the prestigious Shimizu,</i>

09:45.850 --> 09:47.880
<i>Tsubasa can't even move an inch!</i>

09:47.880 --> 09:49.560
<i>This must be quite the ordeal for you, Tsubasa.</i>

09:49.560 --> 09:53.100
<i>The more your skills are recognized, the more enemies you make.</i>

09:53.100 --> 09:54.860
Over here, Tsubasa!

09:55.810 --> 09:56.320
What?!

09:57.360 --> 10:01.620
Since you all keep marking Tsubasa, we're all free out here!

10:02.000 --> 10:02.970
Got it!

10:02.970 --> 10:05.120
<i>Nankatsu connects a quick series of passes!</i>

10:05.120 --> 10:09.580
<i>Through the opening Tsubasa created, the ball quickly gets to Kisugi in front of the goal!</i>

10:09.580 --> 10:11.790
<i>He shoots uncontested!</i>

10:12.400 --> 10:14.750
<i>He has it!</i>

10:14.750 --> 10:15.800
Oh!

10:15.800 --> 10:17.510
Nice catch, Captain!

10:18.250 --> 10:23.240
<i>Shimizu's goalkeeper, their captain Kawakami's excellent diving catch!</i>

10:23.240 --> 10:28.270
If Nankatsu has Wakabayashi, then Shimizu has me, Kawakami!

10:30.520 --> 10:34.020
<i>That goalkeeper ain't half bad.</i>

10:34.020 --> 10:36.020
Tsubasa!

10:36.020 --> 10:40.030
All right, then. We'll finish this talk when the match is over.

10:40.030 --> 10:41.950
Move up!

10:44.790 --> 10:47.370
<i>This has turned into quite the struggle!</i>

10:47.370 --> 10:48.910
<i>Their strength is on par!</i>

10:48.910 --> 10:53.460
<i>They aren't giving each other an inch. This feels like a showdown between champions!</i>

10:54.200 --> 10:55.170
Got it.

10:55.170 --> 10:58.130
<i>Shimizu takes a shot from mid-range!</i>

10:59.340 --> 11:02.180
<i>But Nankatsu has no intention of conceding a goal here!</i>

11:03.850 --> 11:08.310
<i>Wakabayashi is in top form today. He's clearly prepared for this match!</i>

11:09.300 --> 11:12.020
<i>The whistle is blown!</i>

11:12.020 --> 11:15.020
<i>The 20 minutes of the first half are over. The score remains 0-0!</i>

11:17.280 --> 11:21.280
<i>As long as I'm here, I won't let Nankatsu's goal be crushed!</i>

11:21.280 --> 11:23.780
<i>Why is he getting carried away like that?</i>

11:23.780 --> 11:26.320
<i>If this is how it's going to be, we'll have to do it... </i>

11:41.840 --> 11:43.720
Well, that's Shimizu for you.

11:43.720 --> 11:44.570
Yeah.

11:44.570 --> 11:46.180
They're tough.

11:46.180 --> 11:48.480
Well suited for final match opponents, huh?

11:48.480 --> 11:49.430
Exactly.

11:49.430 --> 11:52.680
I'm counting on you guys! Just get one goal.

11:52.680 --> 11:55.600
If we can just score once, we can win.

11:55.600 --> 11:56.880
That might be the case, actually,

11:56.880 --> 11:59.610
but Tsubasa will probably still be completely marked in the second half.

11:59.610 --> 12:02.690
Anyways, you're to get a goal on your own.

12:02.690 --> 12:03.610
Yes, sir!

12:03.610 --> 12:06.320
We've come this far. There's no way we'd lose here!

12:06.320 --> 12:07.120
Right!

12:07.120 --> 12:09.270
We'll be the ones going to the Nationals!

12:09.270 --> 12:10.120
Yeah.

12:10.120 --> 12:11.760
Alright, let's win!

12:11.760 --> 12:14.100
Yeah!

12:14.100 --> 12:17.130
I'll definitely score a goal in the second half.

12:17.130 --> 12:19.630
Tsubasa...

12:19.630 --> 12:21.960
Yeah, I'm counting on you.

12:21.960 --> 12:23.170
You do that.

12:25.340 --> 12:27.930
We will thoroughly mark Tsubasa in the second half as well.

12:27.930 --> 12:31.800
But if we can't score, we won't be able to participate in the Nationals.

12:31.800 --> 12:35.440
To achieve that, we'll execute our plan—

12:36.540 --> 12:38.610
We'll crush Wakabayashi!

12:39.340 --> 12:42.190
If we can keep the focal point of their offense, Tsubasa, down,

12:42.190 --> 12:47.360
and then crush the pillar of the defense, Wakabayashi, then victory will be ours!

12:47.360 --> 12:51.620
Lucky for us, there's no way Wakabayashi's injury has healed yet.

12:51.620 --> 12:55.780
All right! Let's go! We'll be the ones going to the National tournament!

12:55.780 --> 12:56.870
Yeah!

13:00.490 --> 13:04.380
That's right! I'll go and talk to that girl again, before half-time's over.

13:05.100 --> 13:07.440
That girl sure was cute!

13:07.440 --> 13:10.480
It's night and day when you compare her to the boss!

13:10.480 --> 13:12.320
I heard that!

13:12.320 --> 13:13.700
That said—

13:15.080 --> 13:16.560
She's not there!

13:16.560 --> 13:18.590
Where did she go?

13:18.590 --> 13:20.860
Where could she have gone?

13:24.000 --> 13:26.470
<i>The second half begins!</i>

13:29.740 --> 13:31.990
<i>The score was still 0-0 at the end of the first half.</i>

13:31.990 --> 13:35.120
<i>Will Shimizu or Nankatsu be the first to score? </i>

13:35.120 --> 13:38.120
Fight! Fight! Shimizu!

13:38.120 --> 13:41.630
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

13:42.310 --> 13:45.640
<i>Unlike in the first half, Shimizu's passing the ball around carefully.</i>

13:45.640 --> 13:49.140
<i>Are they trying to break Nankatsu's defensive line?</i>

13:49.530 --> 13:51.840
<i>On the other side, Tsubasa is marked by three men,</i>

13:51.840 --> 13:53.910
<i>just like in the first half.</i>

13:53.910 --> 13:56.020
I've got to hand it to them... they're persistent.

13:57.520 --> 13:59.940
Kishida, move more to the left!

14:00.770 --> 14:02.660
That's enough!

14:02.660 --> 14:05.860
<i>Wakabayashi continues to direct the defense, as usual.</i>

14:07.960 --> 14:09.730
Well then, shall we start the plan?

14:11.580 --> 14:15.370
<i>Suddenly, Shimizu sends a long ball toward the goal!</i>

14:16.910 --> 14:19.830
<i>The entire Shimizu team is gunning for the ball!</i>

14:19.830 --> 14:22.460
<i>The high ball starts to fall towards the goal!</i>

14:22.460 --> 14:23.750
Leave it to me!

14:23.750 --> 14:25.550
<i>Wakabayashi comes out for it!</i>

14:28.130 --> 14:30.180
<i>They are all coming straight towards the ball!</i>

14:30.430 --> 14:34.680
<i>Wakabayashi jumps! What physical ability!</i>

14:34.680 --> 14:38.270
<i>Shimizu still dash towards the goal, unfazed!</i>

14:39.210 --> 14:40.520
<i>They crash into him!</i>

14:41.530 --> 14:42.020
What?!

14:45.480 --> 14:47.070
<i>That's quite a foul!</i>

14:47.070 --> 14:48.840
What a play!

14:48.840 --> 14:51.070
It feels like they targeted the keeper, not the ball...

14:51.070 --> 14:55.080
Damn it! You guys did that on purpose, didn't you?

14:55.080 --> 14:56.970
Hey, no hard feelings, all right?

14:56.970 --> 15:00.160
We're desperate to get to the Nationals.

15:00.160 --> 15:01.920
Are you all right? Wakabayashi!

15:01.920 --> 15:06.170
Of course! There's no way I'd lose to that kind of attack!

15:06.170 --> 15:07.630
Wakabayashi...!

15:07.630 --> 15:10.000
Everybody, I'm counting on you for that first goal!

15:10.000 --> 15:11.130
Yeah!

15:12.190 --> 15:15.050
Guess Wakabayashi's healed now, huh?

15:15.050 --> 15:18.140
<i>The game restarts with Nankatsu's free kick!</i>

15:18.140 --> 15:19.240
Let's go!

15:22.650 --> 15:23.770
Urgh!

15:23.770 --> 15:25.290
<i>That's a bad kick!</i>

15:25.290 --> 15:26.790
<i>What's wrong, Wakabayashi?!</i>

15:26.790 --> 15:28.870
<i>He's not able to stand up!</i>

15:28.870 --> 15:31.070
Wakabayashi, is your leg still—

15:31.070 --> 15:32.590
It's a chance! Attack!

15:32.590 --> 15:34.910
The second part of the plan is a success!

15:34.910 --> 15:37.880
Keep possession! It's over if we lose the ball!

15:38.640 --> 15:39.660
Damn it!

15:41.910 --> 15:42.630
Kanda!

15:42.630 --> 15:44.420
<i>Shimizu steals the ball!</i>

15:44.420 --> 15:45.290
That's bad!

15:45.290 --> 15:47.000
We'll score first!!

15:47.000 --> 15:48.840
<i>The cross makes its way in!</i>

15:48.840 --> 15:49.840
This goal's mine!

15:50.620 --> 15:52.090
Such an injury—

15:52.540 --> 15:55.340
<i>Wakabayashi jumps, despite his injury!</i>

15:56.160 --> 15:58.180
<i>He loses his balance!</i>

15:58.180 --> 16:00.640
<i>Will Shimizu score first?!</i>

16:01.440 --> 16:04.100
<i>No! Misaki clears the ball at the line!</i>

16:04.100 --> 16:05.610
Nice, Misaki!

16:05.610 --> 16:08.860
<i>But it's still dangerous! The ball goes directly to Kato!</i>

16:08.860 --> 16:11.900
All right, now—eat this!

16:12.380 --> 16:14.910
<i>The shot is aimed at the immobile Wakabayashi's goal!</i>

16:14.910 --> 16:16.160
Will he be able to catch it?!

16:16.160 --> 16:17.280
It's on the mark!

16:17.280 --> 16:20.370
<i>Will Shimizu FC score first?!</i>

16:20.370 --> 16:24.210
Damn you! Don't you dare take Genzo Wakabayashi so lightly!

16:24.750 --> 16:28.120
<i>He catches it! Wakabayashi jumps towards the ball to catch it!</i>

16:28.120 --> 16:29.710
<i>He makes his last stand!</i>

16:32.110 --> 16:34.380
Take this, Tsubasa!

16:34.760 --> 16:37.250
<i>Wakabayashi kicks the ball away with his injured leg!</i>

16:37.250 --> 16:38.970
<i>It's going a long way forward!</i>

16:38.970 --> 16:41.570
<i>Kicking the ball with my injured leg is better than</i>

16:41.570 --> 16:43.020
<i>using it as my pivot leg...</i>

16:44.100 --> 16:46.150
<i>The pass reaches Tsubasa!</i>

16:46.510 --> 16:50.270
<i>Wakabayashi's tenacity won't go to waste!!</i>

16:50.270 --> 16:51.610
Don't let him get past us!

16:51.610 --> 16:52.550
Tsubasa!

16:52.550 --> 16:53.820
I'm counting on you, guys!

16:53.820 --> 16:59.330
<i>No matter how many people they put on him... he's unstoppable right now.</i>

16:59.330 --> 17:02.410
<i>He broke through our B-team all by himself</i>

17:02.410 --> 17:05.410
<i>the first time we played against each other!</i>

17:17.180 --> 17:17.980
What?!

17:17.980 --> 17:20.720
<i>He passed through all of them in an instant!</i>

17:20.720 --> 17:25.590
<i>Just as I promised, I'll score this half, Wakabayashi!</i>

17:25.590 --> 17:28.480
Tsubasa! Finish it with your trademark volley!

17:28.480 --> 17:30.980
<i>Tsubasa takes the shot!</i>

17:33.560 --> 17:34.860
<i>It's in!</i>

17:35.340 --> 17:37.160
<i>Nankatsu takes the lead!</i>

17:37.160 --> 17:38.360
I did it!

17:38.360 --> 17:42.530
<i>Tsubasa finally broke open the score</i>

17:39.870 --> 17:41.700
You did it!

17:42.330 --> 17:43.700
You did it!

17:42.530 --> 17:45.450
<i>with the great efforts made by Wakabayashi! </i>

17:45.450 --> 17:47.520
<i>Thank you, Tsubasa.</i>

17:47.520 --> 17:50.400
<i>I will make sure to defend this one goal.</i>

17:56.060 --> 17:57.550
Damn!

17:57.550 --> 18:00.550
Fight! Fight! Shimizu!

18:00.550 --> 18:04.060
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

18:04.060 --> 18:06.060
All right, let's stretch the lead!

18:06.060 --> 18:08.020
As if we'd lose like this!

18:09.690 --> 18:11.270
<i>Kisugi passes the ball!</i>

18:12.200 --> 18:15.160
<i>They are playing in a cool and collected manner!</i>

18:15.160 --> 18:16.110
Tsubasa!

18:16.110 --> 18:18.780
<i>Misaki whips the ball in!</i>

18:22.280 --> 18:23.870
<i>It's in!</i>

18:23.870 --> 18:26.370
<i>Nankatsu scores a second!</i>

18:26.370 --> 18:28.690
<i>Nankatsu's all fired up after scoring first!</i>

18:28.690 --> 18:31.380
<i>Nankatsu's attack is fierce!</i>

18:32.330 --> 18:34.240
Just like I thought, Tsubasa's still the same!

18:34.240 --> 18:36.850
See, isn't he good? Tsubasa?

18:36.850 --> 18:42.800
Yeah. It beats the original reason I had to come watch the match in Shizuoka.

18:48.430 --> 18:49.910
Pass it here, pass!

18:49.910 --> 18:51.440
Hey, give it here!

18:51.440 --> 18:54.340
Tch! No good. He's not here!

18:54.340 --> 18:57.750
Hyuga, whom did you come to see all the way here?

18:57.750 --> 19:02.200
Before the Nationals, I need to see about two individuals.

19:02.880 --> 19:06.700
One is Nankatsu FC's Wakabayashi.

19:06.700 --> 19:13.970
The second is here in Musashi FC, Jun Misugi from Tojo Academy.

19:13.970 --> 19:15.910
How good is this guy?

19:15.910 --> 19:22.020
Misugi? He's called the Noble of the Field, a genius all-rounder.

19:22.020 --> 19:23.510
Tsubasa!

19:25.200 --> 19:27.890
<i>He caught it! Shimizu is unable to score!</i>

19:29.280 --> 19:33.060
<i>Even with his injury, Wakabayashi's defending the goal with everything he has!</i>

19:33.060 --> 19:37.780
<i>Nankatsu's victory is just a minute away with a two-goal lead!</i>

19:37.780 --> 19:41.360
Don't let your guard down everybody! Tsubasa!

19:41.850 --> 19:46.370
<i>Nankatsu sends the ball to their ace striker, Tsubasa!</i>

19:46.370 --> 19:48.200
Crush him, there's no time left!

19:50.250 --> 19:52.080
<i>I see an opening!</i>

19:56.910 --> 19:58.260
<i>It's in!</i>

19:58.260 --> 20:01.190
<i>Tsubasa's shot to the near post gives them a third goal!</i>

20:02.750 --> 20:04.890
<i>The whistle blows and the match ends here!</i>

20:04.890 --> 20:08.180
<i>It is Nankatsu FC's victory, with a 3-0 score! </i>

20:08.180 --> 20:09.430
We did it!

20:09.430 --> 20:13.190
<i>The team representing Shizuoka prefecture</i>

20:13.190 --> 20:15.440
<i>in the national tournament will be Nankatsu FC!</i>

20:16.070 --> 20:19.760
<i>With his last goal, Tsubasa has recorded a hat-trick</i>

20:19.760 --> 20:24.520
<i>in every single match of the prefectural tournament!</i>

20:24.520 --> 20:27.240
<i>You do score goals like a charm.</i>

20:28.480 --> 20:34.520
In the end, we weren't able to stop either Tsubasa or Wakabayashi.

20:34.520 --> 20:36.140
It can't be helped.

20:36.140 --> 20:39.590
They were just better than us in every single way.

20:40.330 --> 20:42.880
It's a complete loss.

20:42.880 --> 20:48.890
Tsubasa! Do your best as Shizuoka's rep in the Nationals!

20:49.670 --> 20:52.640
Kawakami! Yeah!

20:52.640 --> 20:55.020
They did it, boss!

20:55.020 --> 20:56.040
Yep!

20:56.040 --> 20:59.760
Tsubasa! Congratulations on the win!

20:59.760 --> 21:01.150
There she is again!

21:01.150 --> 21:04.400
We'll see each other the next time in the Nationals!

21:04.400 --> 21:06.400
I transferred and am now the

21:06.400 --> 21:10.410
manager of Tokyo representatives, Musashi FC!

21:11.550 --> 21:13.180
That young boy is...

21:13.180 --> 21:15.120
Coach, do you know him?

21:15.690 --> 21:20.120
Jun Misugi, he's a player whose potential

21:20.120 --> 21:22.250
in junior football is heavily recognized.

21:22.250 --> 21:24.760
<i>Jun Misugi.</i>

21:24.760 --> 21:26.880
See you later!

21:26.880 --> 21:29.260
She's a manager!

21:29.260 --> 21:33.250
If that's the case, then I'll become the manager for Nankatsu FC, too!

21:33.250 --> 21:33.960
What?

21:33.960 --> 21:37.670
That way I can go with Tsubasa to the national tournament!

21:37.670 --> 21:38.520
God help her.

21:39.660 --> 21:42.550
<i>The curtain closes on the Shizuoka prefecture tournament,</i>

21:42.550 --> 21:46.360
<i>with the winning team being Nankatsu FC.</i>

21:48.410 --> 21:51.700
<i>The Bay Coast Football Stadium awaits</i>

21:51.700 --> 21:56.370
<i>the young boys to come play their football.</i>

22:01.380 --> 22:03.380
You did it, Tsubasa.

22:03.380 --> 22:04.760
Yeah.

22:04.760 --> 22:06.880
Now it's time for the Nationals.

22:06.880 --> 22:09.920
It all begins here.

22:09.920 --> 22:12.350
Yep! All right!

22:13.360 --> 22:17.160
<i>Once I win the National tournament, I'll go</i>

22:17.160 --> 22:18.960
<i>to Brazil, the nation of football, with Roberto! </i>

22:38.870 --> 22:44.750
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.870 --> 22:44.750
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.750 --> 22:50.760
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.750 --> 22:50.760
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.760 --> 22:56.770
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.760 --> 22:56.770
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.770 --> 23:02.230
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.770 --> 23:02.230
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.190 --> 23:08.360
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.190 --> 23:08.360
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.280 --> 23:15.080
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.280 --> 23:15.080
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.080 --> 23:21.120
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.120 --> 23:26.130
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.120 --> 23:26.130
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.420 --> 23:33.300
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.420 --> 23:33.300
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.300 --> 23:39.180
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.180 --> 23:46.070
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.180 --> 23:46.070
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.150 --> 24:00.720
COMING UP, EPISODE 13:
AND THEN, THE NATIONALS
